  <div class="page prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Local relationships</p>
    <h1>Displays and Partners</h1>
    <p class="lede">Red River Gorge Hiker is developing local relationships that place regional photography in settings connected to hikers, visitors, food, conversation, and the landscape itself.</p>

    <section>
      <h2>The Hungry Hiker</h2>
      <p>The Hungry Hiker has approved a planned display of <em>Double Rainbow at Eagle’s Point Buttress</em> as a special physical donation produced independently by Ryan. The photograph remains an approved planned display until it has been physically delivered and installed.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Red River Rockhouse</h2>
      <p>Red River Rockhouse has expressed verbal approval or interest in a small collection of Ryan-produced physical photographs. The relationship remains under development. Inventory is not represented as currently installed or for sale there because quantities, prices, commission terms, payment procedures, placement, permissions, and inventory responsibility have not been documented.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Online orders remain separate</h2>
      <p>Online product selection, payment, production, framing when selected, fulfillment, shipping, and ordinary order service are handled through Fine Art America. A local display or physical-print pilot is separate from online Fine Art America fulfillment.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
